# XO Space — environment variables
#
# Every key, documented. You normally do not copy this file: on first run,
# install.sh writes ./.env for you with laptop-friendly values (marked
# "installer:" below) and never rewrites it afterwards. The literal values
# here are the hosted-container defaults; on a laptop prefer the installer's.
#
# Precedence, lowest to highest: this file's defaults in code → .env →
# variables exported in your shell → the Setup tab's runtime.env / secrets.env.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
HOST=0.0.0.0                    # installer: 127.0.0.1 (loopback only). 0.0.0.0 to reach it from other machines
PORT=5002                       # under STAGE=local, 5003 is used if 5002 is busy
STAGE=beta                      # beta = hosted container paths | local = find CLIs with `which`. installer: local
UVICORN_RELOAD=false            # true = restart on code changes (development only)

# Install nothing beyond requirements.txt. Set to 0 to let the boot hooks
# apt-install, fetch Node via nvm, and `npm -g` the agent CLI for you.
QUIRQ_SKIP_BOOT_INSTALL=1

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Agent backend
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which agent handles chat: claude_code | codex | openclaw | hermes | antigravity.
# The active manifest is resolved AGENT_NAME → DEFAULT_AGENT → the sole
# installed manifest → the openclaw safe-boot default. Set AGENT_NAME to
# switch backends without editing DEFAULT_AGENT.
AGENT_NAME=openclaw             # installer: claude_code
# DEFAULT_AGENT=openclaw

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Paths
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The XO root: your workspace. Every direct sub-folder is a project.
# Surfaced by /api/config/workspace; created on first read if missing.
XO_PROJECTS_ROOT=/home/coder/xo-projects   # installer: the directory you ran it from

# Machine-local state — runtime.env, secrets.env, watcher cursors/locks/
# activity, quirq.log. Must NOT be inside a project folder.
#
# It also roots the per-project RUNTIME tier at <QUIRQ_STATE_ROOT>/projects/<key>/
# (stats, timeline, sync state, session index), keyed by .xo/project.json:pid.
# That tier is machine-local and never synced, so keeping it under this one root
# means `rm -rf` here is still a clean total reset. There is deliberately no
# separate runtime-root variable to set.
QUIRQ_STATE_ROOT=/home/coder/.quirq        # installer: ./.quirq inside XO_PROJECTS_ROOT

# Working directory the agent subprocess starts in, and the directory it is
# allowed to add (--add-dir). Usually the same as XO_PROJECTS_ROOT.
AI_WORKSPACE_ROOT=/home/coder              # installer: same as XO_PROJECTS_ROOT

# What the watcher tails to build Sessions and the workspace views:
#   active = only AGENT_NAME's session store
#   all    = every installed agent's store, so Sessions shows them side by side
QUIRQ_WATCHER_SOURCE_MODE=active           # installer: all

# Directory the Remote Control session (`claude remote-control`) starts in.
# Default: ~ so a phone/web session can reach everything under it.
XO_RC_DIR=/home/coder

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Agent CLIs and credentials
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave credentials COMMENTED rather than blank: `KEY=` sets an empty string,
# which overrides the server's own default instead of falling back to it.
# You can also enter them in the Setup tab instead of here.

CLAUDE_CLI_PATH=claude          # path to the claude binary; bare name = on PATH
CLAUDE_TIMEOUT=300              # seconds
CLAUDE_PERMISSION_MODE=bypassPermissions
# Claude auth: a native login (`claude auth login`, or "Connect Claude" in
# Setup) always wins and self-refreshes. These two are only passed to the
# CLI when there is no native login — an explicit API-billing alternative.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-api-key
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

CODEX_CLI_PATH=codex
CODEX_TIMEOUT=300               # default: inherits CLAUDE_TIMEOUT
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key
# CODEX_API_KEY=your-codex-api-key   # per-run auth for `codex exec`

# Legacy Plane-A provider for /ask_question*: claude | codex
AI_PROVIDER=claude

# Agent-native behaviour is configured in the project, not here:
#   Claude Code — CLAUDE.md and .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md
#   Codex       — AGENTS.md and .agents/skills/*/SKILL.md

# OpenClaw local gateway (spawned by config/agents/openclaw/agent.sh on :18789)
OPENCLAW_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18789/v1/chat/completions
OPENCLAW_MODEL=openclaw/default
# OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN=xo-cowork   # Bearer for the gateway; must match what it was started with

# Hermes local gateway (`hermes gateway run` on :8642). Needs
# API_SERVER_ENABLED=true and API_SERVER_KEY in ~/.hermes/.env; the value
# here must match. Hermes owns session history in ~/.hermes/state.db — the
# server sends the session id via X-Hermes-Session-Id and stays stateless.
# HERMES_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8642/v1/chat/completions
# HERMES_MODEL=hermes-agent
# API_SERVER_KEY=change-me-local-dev

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# XO account (optional — everything local works without it)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Long-lived Clerk user API key. Links this install to your XO account.
# Usage is reported ONLY when this key is set and valid: token counts, costs
# and session/tool counts once a day — never prompts or file contents.
# Empty, missing or invalid: nothing is tracked. See README "What leaves
# your machine".
# XO_API_KEY=ak_xxxxxxxx

# Upstream API (default is fine). xo-swarm-api owns authentication; this server only
# holds the credential it uses for its own outbound calls.
CHAT_API_BASE_URL=https://api-swarm-beta.xo.builders
XO_AUTH_START_PATH=/auth/browser/start
XO_AUTH_STATUS_PATH=/auth/browser/status
XO_AUTH_CONSUME_PATH=/auth/browser/consume
XO_GET_USER_ID_PATH=/get-user-id

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project sharing (commit relay). Always on; nothing to switch on.
# The relay polls xo-swarm-api once a minute for repos shared with this
# workspace and git-fetches their new commits; it reports this workspace's
# own pushes on shared repos as commit hashes (never file contents). It PARKS
# (zero network calls) unless XO_SPACE_ID is set AND the install is signed
# in (XO_API_KEY or the in-app sign-in). Per-repo bookmarks live in
# <state>/project_sharing/, never inside a project.
# XO_SPACE_ID=                       # this workspace's id at the swarm
# PROJECT_SHARING_ENABLED=true                   # emergency brake only
# PROJECT_SHARING_WATCH_BRANCH=main              # branch watched / reported
# PROJECT_SHARING_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=60       # one flat cadence, min 5
# PROJECT_SHARING_POLL_JITTER_RATIO=0.2          # 60s becomes 48-72s so a fleet spreads out
# Repos shared with this workspace are cloned into the XO root automatically
# (one at a time, never over an existing folder, nothing from the repo is run).
# Private repos need the GitHub connector in Setup; until then the Files tab
# says "needs GitHub sign-in" and shows the manual clone command.
# PROJECT_SHARING_AUTO_CLONE=true                # kill-switch
# PROJECT_SHARING_CLONE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=600
# If both are set, the server consumes the browser-auth session once at
# startup; otherwise they are fallbacks for a /xo-auth/consume body.
# XO_AUTH_SESSION_ID=your-auth-session-id
# XO_POLL_TOKEN=your-poll-token

# Hour (UTC) of the daily usage sync when signed in. Debug: USAGE_SYNC_DEBUG=true
# plus USAGE_SYNC_DEBUG_INTERVAL_MINUTES for a faster loop.
# USAGE_SYNC_HOUR_UTC=2

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Connectors
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credential stores live in the user's config directory, not the checkout, so
# they survive a redeploy and a checkout never carries secrets. A store left at
# an older in-checkout location is moved to the new default on first access.

# GitHub / Vercel / Manus token store. Default: ~/.config/token.json
# MCP_TOKENS_FILE=~/.config/token.json

# Vercel OAuth — must match the redirect_uri registered in the Vercel OAuth app.
# VERCEL_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1/callback

# rclone (Google Drive, OneDrive): config file and the OAuth callback port
# shared by both connectors. Default: ~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf
# RCLONE_CONFIG=~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf
# RCLONE_OAUTH_PORT=53682

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Composio (Gmail, Google Workspace, Notion, Figma) — /api/connectors/composio/*
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE CREDENTIALS ARE NOT SET HERE, AND NEVER TOUCH THIS PROCESS. COMPOSIO_API_KEY and
# the eight COMPOSIO_AUTH_CONFIG_<TOOLKIT> ids live only in xo-swarm-api's environment.
# Every Composio SDK call — connect, list/disconnect connections, list tools, create or
# update the tool-router session — runs inside xo-swarm-api itself, authenticated as
# whoever called it (the same XO credential, XO_API_KEY, already used for /usage/report
# and /auth/workspace-principal); this server only ever calls xo-swarm-api's narrow
# per-operation routes under /connectors/composio/*, never the raw key. A workspace
# therefore has no Composio secret to leak, and rotating the key is one change on the
# swarm. There is no local escape hatch (no COMPOSIO_CREDENTIALS_SOURCE=env): a
# self-hosted install with its own Composio project needs its own xo-swarm-api.
#
# Composio is addressed by your bare XO account id, so a connection made in ONE workspace
# is visible to all of them. Which of them a given workspace may actually use is chosen
# per workspace on the Connectors tab and enforced in the Composio session — nothing is
# enabled in a new workspace until someone turns it on. See DEVELOPING.md §10.2 and §10.4.
#
# Nothing below is a secret. What stays here is per-deployment behaviour.

# Where the provider redirects after OAuth. Per deployment, so it stays here.
# Must match this server's public origin AND be registered as an allowed callback
# on the shared auth configs in the Composio dashboard — they are org-wide now, so
# every origin that will connect has to be listed there.
# Required: there is no built-in default. Unset, /connect answers 422 naming this
# variable instead of handing out an auth_url that redirects nowhere.
COMPOSIO_CALLBACK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5002/api/connectors/composio/callback

# Optional. Let one account use several connections of the same toolkit (work and
# personal Gmail) in a single agent session. Off means Composio's default: one
# account per toolkit, the most recently connected one. Connecting a second
# account still works with this off — it just replaces which one the agent sees.
# COMPOSIO_MULTI_ACCOUNT=1

# Optional. When on, an agent facing several active accounts for a toolkit must
# name one (`account`: a connected-account id or an alias) in the tool call
# instead of silently getting the newest. Default off.
# COMPOSIO_MULTI_ACCOUNT_REQUIRE_SELECTION=1

# Optional. TTL (seconds) for this server's local record of the session ids
# minted by xo-swarm-api and served through GET /xo-auth/session/self. Also read
# as the default TTL on the swarm side. Default 12h.
# XO_SESSION_TTL=43200

# Optional. Scratch root for the per-turn Claude Code --mcp-config files,
# swept at boot. Default /tmp/xo-cowork.
# XO_MCP_TMP_ROOT=/tmp/xo-cowork

# Optional. Seconds between the background sweeps that keep every capable agent's
# MCP config pointed at this workspace's Composio proxy. The sweep also runs at
# boot (retrying while XO is unreachable) and whenever the Connectors tab loads;
# there is no manual install. 0 disables only the periodic pass. Default 600.
# COMPOSIO_MCP_RECONCILE_INTERVAL=600

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# xo-projects backup & restore (POST /api/xo-projects-sync/...)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Populated by POST /api/xo-projects-sync/setup — you usually don't edit
# these by hand. They're written here so dotenv picks them up after a
# server restart and so a workspace can be re-provisioned from this file.
#
# BACKUP_REPO_NAME — the private GitHub repo that holds the encrypted
#   snapshots (one repo for all projects). Owner comes from the GitHub token.
# BACKUP_REPO_NAME=xo-projects-backup
#
# BACKUP_PASSWORD — symmetric gpg passphrase. Required on every backup AND
#   every restore — without it your backups are unrecoverable.
# BACKUP_PASSWORD=change-me-to-a-strong-passphrase
#
# GITHUB_PAT — fallback GitHub token when the GitHub connector isn't set up.
#   Needs `repo` scope. The connector token takes precedence when both exist.
# GITHUB_PAT=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# Requires gnupg (gpg + gpg-agent) on the host: sudo apt-get install -y gnupg
